# Vercel serves this repository's root as the website (vercel.json has
# "outputDirectory": "."), so any file here can be downloaded from the live
# site unless it is listed below. The audits matter most: each one describes
# security gaps that have not been fixed yet.
/audits
/.claude
/.github
/scripts
/scratch
# The test suites and tools, including the rules probes that document the
# holes still open.
/tests
/tools
/CLAUDE.md
/FEATURES.md

# Local secrets. Git never has them, but `vercel deploy` from this folder
# uploads everything not excluded here, and Vercel's own defaults skip
# .env.local but not .env.
/.env
/.env.*
# The local config.js can hold a live AI key. Keep the leading slash: a
# bare "config.js" would also drop api/config.js, the function that serves
# the public Firebase config and must stay deployed.
/config.js

# Downloaded keys, mirrored from .gitignore. Git keeps them out of the repo,
# but `vercel deploy` uploads the working folder. Google names a
# service-account download after the project and key id
# (techable-tts-1a2b3c4d.json), which matches nothing obvious, so the root
# deploys only the .json files that belong there. vercel.json stays allowed:
# it is the deployment's own configuration.
/*.json
!/firestore.indexes.json
!/firebase.json
!/vercel.json
# And the obvious names, for a key dropped in a subdirectory instead.
*-key.json
*credential*.json
*service-account*.json
*serviceaccount*.json
gcp-*.json
*.pem
*.p12
# Firebase emulator logs (firebase-debug.log, firestore-debug.log, ...).
*-debug.log
